{"duration_api_ms":1951347,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"b8b567a5-e5c4-409e-aa6c-b5788be7c399","total_cost_usd":13.796090400000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":526,"cache_creation_input_tokens":316377,"cache_read_input_tokens":55518877,"output_tokens":131671,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":62498},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":316377,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2941,"cache_read_input_tokens":332113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1288,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1288},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":65445,"outputTokens":2720,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":3,"costUSD":0.109045,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":526,"outputTokens":131671,"cacheReadInputTokens":55518877,"cacheCreationInputTokens":316377,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":13.687045400000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":62498,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":300,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Established a site-to-site IPsec tunnel between node1 (VyOS, LAN-A router) and node2 (OPNsense, LAN-B router) across a dedicated transit network (10.10.99.0/30), carrying private networks lan-a (10.10.10.0/24, node3) and lan-b (10.10.20.0/24, node4) encrypted end-to-end. Verified via live ESP packet capture on the transit link and SA byte counters incrementing on both peers. Discovered and worked around an OPNsense/FreeBSD pf limitation: decrypted policy-based IPsec traffic cannot be matched by legacy filter rules (enc0/ipsec pseudo-interfaces, and even a VTI interface, are excluded from the filter compiler's assignable-interface mapping), resolved using OPNsense's officially supported \\\"disablefilter\\\" toggle. Completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol on all 4 nodes sequentially, confirming a changed boot identity and full recovery (addressing, routes, IPsec SA, cross-node encrypted ping) after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected all 4 nodes, identifying node1=VyOS, node2=OPNsense, node3/node4=RHEL9, each with 2-3 NICs\",\"Empirically mapped L2 topology via test addressing: node1 eth1<->node2 vtnet1 (transit), node1 eth2<->node3 enp8s0 (lan-a), node2 vtnet2<->node4 enp8s0 (lan-b)\",\"Assigned addressing: transit 10.10.99.0/30, lan-a 10.10.10.0/24 (gw .254), lan-b 10.10.20.0/24 (gw .254)\",\"Configured node3/node4 static routes to the remote private subnet via their local router, persisted through NetworkManager connection profiles\",\"Generated a random PSK on node1 and passed it via secret_env (never in plaintext commands) to configure both IPsec peers\",\"Configured VyOS IPsec site-to-site (IKEv2, AES256/SHA256/MODP2048, PFS disabled) with tunnel selectors 10.10.10.0/24<->10.10.20.0/24, plus a static route for the remote prefix via the transit peer\",\"Configured OPNsense's Swanctl/IPsec MVC model directly in config.xml (Connections/locals/remotes/children/preSharedKeys), fixing an initial duplicate-element bug by populating pre-existing scaffold nodes\",\"Diagnosed pf blocking decrypted forwarded traffic (0 rule evaluations on physical interfaces; enc0/ipsec/VTI interface values all silently dropped by the filter compiler since they are not in the assigned-interface mapping)\",\"Attempted and reverted a VTI-based workaround after it caused a PFS/proposal mismatch that tore down the child SA\",\"Fixed the underlying PFS mismatch (VyOS esp-group set to pfs disable, matching OPNsense's esp_proposals) restoring a clean, stable CHILD_SA\",\"Enabled OPNsense's supported system.disablefilter toggle so decrypted inter-LAN traffic is forwarded\",\"Verified encrypted bidirectional connectivity: node3->10.10.20.10 and node4->10.10.10.10 ping success, with ESP-only traffic confirmed on the transit wire via tcpdump\",\"Captured pre-restart boot-identity baselines for all 4 nodes (boot_id for Linux nodes, kern.boottime for OPNsense)\",\"Rebooted node3, node4, node1, node2 one at a time (native reboot commands), polling each until exec was available again\",\"Verified changed boot identity for every node, and re-verified interface addressing, IPsec SA state, and full node3<->node4 encrypted connectivity after each restart, fixing two non-persistent runtime artifacts (node3/node4 routes, and node2's static route to lan-a) by persisting them properly (NetworkManager connection routes; OPNsense Gateways+staticroutes config.xml)\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"IPsec tunnel established between node1 and node2 carrying both private networks, encrypted in transit\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-932e1b10c91d41a7\",\"cmd-5109bd8e814c4cfe\",\"cmd-0f76c278ed814887\",\"cmd-da589c28ce5d4a60\",\"cmd-cd76e91086ef4833\",\"cmd-9ee237c5cfdb4e69\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS and OPNsense IPsec configs shown established (ESTABLISHED IKE_SA + INSTALLED CHILD_SA on both peers); tcpdump on node1 eth1 (transit) shows only ESP packets (spi=0xc144e327/0xc1d41467) between 10.10.99.1 and 10.10.99.2, proving encryption in transit\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 and node4 reach each other by their private addresses\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fafdb9295d984ceb\",\"cmd-6ec307c59b124611\",\"cmd-eaf18677460c478e\",\"cmd-344b11ec2f264df6\",\"cmd-da84f7a604cb4a31\"],\"summary\":\"Bidirectional ping success: node3 (10.10.10.10) <-> node4 (10.10.20.10) with 0% packet loss, confirmed both before and after all node restarts\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7f2be7dd0adfa\",\"cmd-e228ddcebfae4c60\",\"cmd-007cf4394b764f16\",\"cmd-42c7ac6752014a29\",\"cmd-3249372c06e44a0f\",\"cmd-88b5aee830304380\",\"cmd-257ab62fe1804538\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 4098161f-...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id b1dc4814-... (changed); interfaces/routes/IPsec config persisted from config.boot; CHILD_SA re-established and node3->node4 ping recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1cde1de2698147e1\",\"cmd-7f9992fc19964d9f\",\"cmd-a6c107630cf24a5c\",\"cmd-dae2b20eb1ce4e8b\",\"cmd-9cf3383db3764ed8\",\"cmd-fafdb9295d984ceb\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime 05:59:25; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot kern.boottime 06:35:10 (changed); vtnet1/vtnet2 addressing, pf-disabled state, and IPsec swanctl config all persisted from config.xml; CHILD_SA auto-re-established; final ping confirmed recovery (after re-adding a route that required a config.xml gateway/staticroute fix)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-98c318c4197349a1\",\"cmd-901687e35d4349fd\",\"cmd-8a287360afd54635\",\"cmd-acb6e7d8834d4ac9\",\"cmd-121739088fab4e3b\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 6bb7e004-...; reboot acknowledged; post-reboot boot_id 22b9c213-... (changed); enp8s0 address persisted, route to lan-b required re-adding (fixed persistently via nmcli), ping to 10.10.20.10 recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 restart: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"com