oth IPsec peers","Configured VyOS IPsec site-to-site (IKEv2, AES256/SHA256/MODP2048, PFS disabled) with tunnel selectors 10.10.10.0/24<->10.10.20.0/24, plus a static route for the remote prefix via the transit peer","Configured OPNsense's Swanctl/IPsec MVC model directly in config.xml (Connections/locals/remotes/children/preSharedKeys), fixing an initial duplicate-element bug by populating pre-existing scaffold nodes","Diagnosed pf blocking decrypted forwarded traffic (0 rule evaluations on physical interfaces; enc0/ipsec/VTI interface values all silently dropped by the filter compiler since they are not in the assigned-interface mapping)","Attempted and reverted a VTI-based workaround after it caused a PFS/proposal mismatch that tore down the child SA","Fixed the underlying PFS mismatch (VyOS esp-group set to pfs disable, matching OPNsense's esp_proposals) restoring a clean, stable CHILD_SA","Enabled OPNsense's supported system.disablefilter toggle so decrypted inter-LAN traffic is forwarded","Verified encrypted bidirectional connectivity: node3->10.10.20.10 and node4->10.10.10.10 ping success, with ESP-only traffic confirmed on the transit wire via tcpdump","Captured pre-restart boot-identity baselines for all 4 nodes (boot_id for Linux nodes, kern.boottime for OPNsense)","Rebooted node3, node4, node1, node2 one at a time (native reboot commands), polling each until exec was available again","Verified changed boot identity for every node, and re-verified interface addressing, IPsec SA state, and full node3<->node4 encrypted connectivity after each restart, fixing two non-persistent runtime artifacts (node3/node4 routes, and node2's static route to lan-a) by persisting them properly (NetworkManager connection routes; OPNsense Gateways+staticroutes config.xml)"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"IPsec tunnel established between node1 and node2 carrying both private networks, encrypted in transit","command_ids":["cmd-932e1b10c91d41a7","cmd-5109bd8e814c4cfe","cmd-0f76c278ed